1. Emergency Procedures — Analytical Dynamics

· Loss of rotation: Magnetic drag deceleration \dot{\omega}_{\text{drag}} = \tau_{\text{drag}}/I \approx 1.1\times10^{-5}\,\text{rad/s}^2. Time to drop below 0.7 g: ~33 h. For rapid braking, a mechanical friction brake applying 3.0\times10^5\,\text{N·m} brings the bowl to rest in 5 min, with a deceleration of 0.07 rad/s² and a tangential jerk of 3.5 m/s², tolerable for restrained occupants.
· Decompression: The bowl is partitioned into six radial pressure cells; thermodynamic venting calculations show that a 10 cm² breach causes cabin pressure to fall to 50 kPa in 120 s, allowing safe egress.
· Medical evacuation: A central hoist with Coriolis‑compensated sling (active gimbal) retrieves crew in ≤3 min, respecting local gravity vector.

