1. Life Support, Power, and Thermal Architecture

10.1 Atmosphere Revitalisation
A Sabatier reactor converts metabolic CO₂ and imported H₂ into CH₄ and H₂O; O₂ is recovered via electrolysis. The mass balance equations are solved analytically for a crew of 8: required H₂ import ≈ 0.45 kg/day. A 4‑bed molecular sieve maintains CO₂ <0.5%.

10.2 Power System
A 100 kWe Kilopower‑derived fast reactor (thermal 1 MW) is sited 500 m away. The electrical power transfer across the rotating interface uses a brushless inductive coupler. The design equations for the rotary transformer yield an efficiency of 95% at 100 kW.

10.3 Thermal Control
Habitat internal heat load (100 kW) is rejected by dome‑mounted radiators. Using the Stefan‑Boltzmann law with emittance \varepsilon = 0.9 and a sky temperature of 150 K, the required area is

A = \frac{Q_{\text{rej}}}{\varepsilon \sigma (T_s^4 - T_{\text{sky}}^4)} \approx 600\,\text{m}^2,

with surface temperature T_s = 300\,\text{K}. A pumped water‑glycol loop conveys heat from the bowl to the stationary radiators via a rotating fluid coupling.

